---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { COMPANY, COMPANY_ADDRESS } from '../config';

// Placeholder for the owner to replace. See LEGAL_IS_PLACEHOLDER in src/config.ts.
const todo = 'To be written';
---

<Legal
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="How MotoPapers collects, uses and protects your personal data."
  updated="Last updated: to be added"
>
  <h2>Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    MotoPapers tracks and renews vehicle papers for drivers in Nigeria. You can reach us at
    {COMPANY_ADDRESS} or on <a href={`tel:${COMPANY.phone.tel}`}>{COMPANY.phone.display}</a>.
    <span class="todo">{todo}</span> the legal name of the company and its registration number.
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <p><span class="todo">{todo}</span> Confirm this list. Likely items:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Your name, email address and phone number.</li>
    <li>
      Your cars: plate number, make, model, colour, engine and chassis numbers, and the photo of the
      vehicle licence you upload.
    </li>
    <li>Your papers: expiry dates and insurance cover type.</li>
    <li>Your delivery address.</li>
    <li>
      Payments and wallet activity. Card and bank details are handled by Paystack; MotoPapers
      doesn't see or store card numbers.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How we use it</h2>
  <p>
    <span class="todo">{todo}</span> For example: tracking expiry dates, sending reminders by SMS and
    email, processing renewals and delivering papers, running your wallet, answering support requests
    and keeping the service secure. State the lawful basis for each.
  </p>

  <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
  <p>
    <span class="todo">{todo}</span> Name each kind of partner and why: Paystack for payments, the agencies
    and insurers that issue renewals, SMS and email providers, and delivery partners. Say that MotoPapers
    doesn't sell personal data, if that's the case.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies and analytics</h2>
  <p>
    <span class="todo">{todo}</span> This website sets no cookies. If analytics are switched on, they
    use Plausible, which counts visits without cookies or personal data. Describe what the app stores
    to keep you signed in.
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>
    <span class="todo">{todo}</span> Retention periods for account, vehicle and payment records.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    <span class="todo">{todo}</span> Under the Nigeria Data Protection Act 2023 you can ask to see, correct
    or delete your data, object to some uses, and complain to the Nigeria Data Protection Commission.
    Explain how to make a request.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    <span class="todo">{todo}</span> The email address for privacy requests and, if you have one, your
    Data Protection Officer.
  </p>
</Legal>
